hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1204","Khattab bin Usman ne hum se bayan kiya, unhon ne kaha: Ismail ne hum se bayan kiya, Muhammad bin Ziyad se, Abu Rashid Hubrani se ke unhon ne kaha: Main Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr ke paas aaya to maine un se kaha: Hamein woh bayan karo jo tum ne Rasoolullah sallallahu alaihi wasallam se suna hai, to unhon ne meri taraf ek sahifa badha diya phir unhon ne kaha: Ye woh hai jo Nabi sallallahu alaihi wasallam ne mere liye likha tha, phir maine us mein dekha to achanak us mein tha: Beshak Hazrat Abu Bakr Siddiq raziyallahu anhu ne Nabi sallallahu alaihi wasallam se sawal kiya, unhon ne kaha: Ya Rasoolallah, mujhe sikhaiye jo main kahun jab main subah karun aur jab main shaam karun, to Aap ne farmaya: Ae Abu Bakr, kaho: Ae Allah, aasmanon aur zameen ko paida karne wale, ghaib aur hazir ko janne wale, har cheez ke Rabb aur Malik, main Teri panah mangta hun apne nafs ke shar se aur shaitan ke shar aur us ke shirk se aur is se ke main apne nafs par koi burai kamaun ya use kisi Musalman ki taraf kheench laaun."
"1205","Hazrat Abu Huraira raziyallahu anhu se riwayat hai ke Nabi sallallahu alaihi wasallam jab subah karte to kehte: Ae Allah, Tere se hum ne subah ki aur Tere se hum ne shaam ki aur Tere se hum jeete hain aur Tere se hum marte hain aur Teri taraf hi uth kar jana hai. Aur jab shaam karte to kehte: Ae Allah, Tere se hum ne shaam ki aur Tere se hum ne subah ki aur Tere se hum jeete hain aur Tere se hum marte hain aur Teri taraf hi lautna hai."
"1206","Hazrat Ibn Umar raziyallahu anhuma se riwayat hai ke Rasoolullah sallallahu alaihi wasallam shaam karte waqt aur subah karte waqt ye dua nahi chhorte the: Ae Allah, beshak main Tujh se duniya aur aakhirat mein aafiyat ka sawal karta hun, Ae Allah, beshak main Tujh se apne deen aur apni duniya aur apne ghar walon aur apne maal mein muafi aur aafiyat ka sawal karta hun, Ae Allah, meri pardadari wali cheezon ko dhaank de aur meri ghabrahaton ko aman de, Ae Allah, meri hifazat farma mere aage se aur mere peeche se aur mere daayen se aur mere baayen se aur mere upar se, aur main Teri azmat ki panah mangta hun is se ke main apne neeche se achanak halak kar diya jaun."
"1207","Hazrat Anas bin Malik raziyallahu anhu ne kaha: Rasoolullah sallallahu alaihi wasallam ne farmaya: Jo shakhs subah karte waqt kahe: Ae Allah, beshak hum ne subah ki aur sara mulk Allah ke liye subah karta hai, aur hum Tujhe gawah banate hain aur Tere arsh uthane walon aur Tere farishton aur Teri tamam makhlooq ko gawah banate hain ke beshak Tu hi Allah hai, Tere siwa koi mabood nahi, Akela, Tera koi shareek nahi, aur beshak Muhammad sallallahu alaihi wasallam Tere bande aur Tere Rasool hain, to Allah azza wa jalla us din us ka chautha hissa aag se azaad farma deta hai, aur jo use do martaba kahe to Allah us ka aadha hissa aag se azaad farma deta hai, aur jo use chaar martaba kahe to Allah use us din poori tarah aag se azaad farma deta hai."
"1208","Hazrat Abu Huraira raziyallahu anhu ne kaha: Hazrat Abu Bakr raziyallahu anhu ne kaha: Ya Rasoolallah, mujhe ek dua sikhaiye jo main subah aur shaam mein mangu. Aap ne farmaya: Kaho: Ae Allah, ghaib aur hazir ke janne wale, aasmanon aur zameen ke paida karne wale, har cheez ke Rabb aur Malik, main gawahi deta hun ke Tere siwa koi mabood nahi, main Teri panah mangta hun apne nafs ke shar se aur shaitan ke shar aur us ke shirk se. Use kaho jab tum subah karo aur jab tum shaam karo aur jab tum apna bistar pakdo."
"1209","Hazrat Abu Huraira raziyallahu anhu se pehli hadith ki manind riwayat hai, aur us mein hai: Nabi sallallahu alaihi wasallam ne farmaya: Har cheez ke Rabb aur Malik. Aur Aap ne ye bhi farmaya: Shaitan ke shar aur us ke shirk se."
